# Python and Node build products. Each project should ignore its own, but a
# repo whose .gitignore is missing must still not be able to commit a virtual
# environment or a dependency tree with one `git add -A`.
.venv/
__pycache__/
node_modules/

.env
.env.*
.env.local
# ...but not the checked-in templates. `.env.*` above matches these too, and
# silently ignoring the example file is how a repo ends up with no documented
# environment at all.
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
!.env.dist

# Scratch files from the nvim 99 plugin. Its tmp_dir is "./tmp", relative to
# the cwd, so these land in whatever project you happen to be editing — and the
# *-prompt files contain excerpts of that project's source. **/ because a
# pattern with a slash in the middle is anchored to the repo root: plain
# tmp/99-* missed every file from an nvim started in a subdirectory.
**/tmp/99-*

**/.claude/settings.local.json
